"""Encoder-variant seam: default output is byte-identical, variants propagate.

The golden digests below were captured from the pre-seam code (commit 8f27812)
by rebuilding every row of ``make_synthetic_anchors`` and hashing the canonical
JSONL bytes.  They are the whole point of this file: if the seam ever perturbs
a single byte of the production encoder's output, these fail.
"""

